0	section	Showing the brooch to the Duke
1	line	Duke Horacio	Greetings. Welcome to my castle.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Have you any quests for me?
1	option	Where can I find money?
1	option	I dug through the rubble...
2	line	Player	I dug through the rubble in the cellar and found a tunnel!
2	line	Player	On the ground I found this brooch.
2	line	Duke Horacio	I've never seen anything like that before. It doesn't come from Lumbridge. What do you think, Sigmund?
2	line	Sigmund	It is unknown to me, your grace. But the fact it is there is enough to prove [NPC]'s story. It must have been dropped by a goblin as it fled.
2	line	Duke Horacio	I've never heard of a goblin wearing something so well-crafted.
2	line	Sigmund	Then it must have been stolen!
2	line	Duke Horacio	But it wasn't stolen from us. Where could it be from?
2	line	Sigmund	That doesn't matter! You said yourself that goblins couldn't have made that, so they must have stolen it from somewhere.
2	line	Sigmund	Horrible, thieving goblins have broken into our cellar! We must retaliate immediately!
2	line	Sigmund	First we should wipe out the goblins east of the river, then we can march on the goblin village to the north-west...
2	line	Duke Horacio	I will not commit troops until I have proof that goblins are behind this.
2	line	Duke Horacio	{player}, please find out what you can about this brooch. The librarian in Varrock might be able to help identify the symbol.
1	action	end
