0	section	The Goblin Generals
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Have you ever heard of the Dorgeshuun?
2	line	Player	Have you ever heard of the Dorgeshuun?
2	line	General Bentnoze	Dorgeshuun? That old goblin legend. Lost tribe.
2	line	General Wartface	In time of much-war there many tribes. Big High War-God send Dorgesh tribe to fight beardy-short-people in mountains.
2	line	General Bentnoze	No no, he send them to fight tall people with biting blades, that what I hear.
2	line	General Wartface	It was beardy-short-people, that how legend go.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Make up your minds!
3	line	Player	Make up your minds!
3	line	General Bentnoze	It was tall people! That what old storyteller say!
3	line	General Wartface	No, beardy-short-people. That how legend always go, stupid.
3	line	General Bentnoze	You stupid!
3	action	other
2	option	Do you want me to decide for you again?
3	line	Player	Do you want me to decide for you again?
3	line	General Bentnoze	That most stupid idea yet. If it happen it either happen one way or the other. You can't just decide which.
3	line	General Wartface	Yeah even goblins know that.
3	action	other
2	option	It doesn't really matter
3	line	Player	It doesn't really matter. What happened to them?
3	line	General Wartface	Well, they say, 'We not want to fight,' so god punish them.
3	line	General Bentnoze	That silly. No goblin ever say that.
3	line	General Wartface	What happen then?
3	line	General Bentnoze	They lose battle, that why god punish them.
3	line	General Wartface	Ha ha! If they lost battle they all be dead!
3	line	General Bentnoze	No no, they losing so they run away, and Big High War-God punish them for running away.
3	select	Select an option
3	option	Who were they fighting again?
4	line	Player	Who were they fighting again?
4	line	General Wartface	It was beardy-short-people in mountains.
4	line	General Bentnoze	No no, it was tall people.
4	action	previous
3	option	What kind of god would punish them for refusing to fight?
4	line	Player	What kind of god would punish them for refusing to fight?
4	line	General Bentnoze	Shh! Must not question Big High War-God!
4	line	General Wartface	No, because he much bigger than us.
4	action	other
3	option	Well either way they refused to fight
4	line	Player	Well either way they refused to fight.
4	line	General Wartface	Yeah I suppose so.
4	line	General Bentnoze	Anyway then Big High War-God punish them. He turn their insides to stone.
4	line	General Wartface	Ha ha ha! That silly!
4	line	General Bentnoze	Not as silly as green armour! What happen then?
4	line	General Wartface	He put them inside stone! Big hole open in ground and they all go into cave.
4	line	General Bentnoze	That not punishment! Caves nice and cool.
4	line	General Wartface	But then he close cave so they not get out! You not want to stay in cave all the time.
4	select	Select an option
4	option	Why were they punished again?
5	line	Player	Why were there punished again?
5	line	General Wartface	It because they run away from fight.
5	line	General Bentnoze	No, it because they refuse to fight night before battle.
5	action	previous
4	option	So do goblins make their own tunnels?
5	line	Player	So do goblins make their own tunnels?
5	line	General Bentnoze	What? Make our own tunnels?
5	line	General Wartface	We hadn't thought of that.
5	action	other
4	option	Well I found a brooch underground...
5	line	Player	Well I found a brooch underground, and I looked up the symbol and it was the symbol of the Dorgeshuun.
5	line	General Bentnoze	That not look like goblin brooch.
5	line	General Wartface	Goblins not wear jewellery.
5	line	General Bentnoze	Well if it Dorgeshuun tribe they not know who won big wars. You should greet them with goblin victory dance!
5	line	General Wartface	No no, you greet them with goblin tribal bow.
5	line	General Bentnoze	Doing bow make you look like a wimp.
5	line	General Wartface	It how tribes greet each other in old days.
5	line	General Bentnoze	Only if they wimpy tribes! Goblin salute strong!
5	select	Select an option
5	option	So why is the Dorgeshuun tribe underground?
