2	line	Sigmund	The priceless Lumbridge Silverware! It comes out only on special occasions. It was kept in storage in the cellar, but now the goblins have stolen it.
2	line	Player	So why did no one notice earlier?
2	line	Sigmund	That doesn't matter. You'll never find it, because the goblins took it. So you can't stop the war!
2	line	Player	Actually I have found it! You put it in the H.A.M. cave!
2	line	Sigmund	I... I... You're lying! I don't know what you're talking about.
2	action	end
1	option	Who are you?
0	section	Returning the silverware
1	line	Duke Horacio	Greetings. Welcome to my castle.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Have you any quests for me?
1	option	Where can I find money?
1	option	I found the missing silverware in the HAM cave!
2	line	Player	I found the missing silverware in the HAM cave!
2	line	Duke Horacio	Sigmund! Is this your doing?
2	line	Sigmund	Of...of course not! The goblins must have, um, dropped the silverware as they ran away.
2	line	Duke Horacio	Don't lie to me! I knew you were a HAM member but I didn't think you would stoop to this. You are dismissed from my service.
2	line	Sigmund	But don't you see it was for the best? For goblins to be living under our feet like this... ugh. It doesn't matter how civilized they are: all sub-human species must be wiped out!
2	line	Duke Horacio	That's enough! Get out of my castle now!
2	line	Duke Horacio	I see I was ill-advised. Unless there is an act of aggression by the cave goblins there is no need for war.
2	box	The Duke writes a document and signs it.
2	line	Duke Horacio	This peace treaty specifies the border between Lumbridge and the Cave Goblin realm. Please take it to the cave goblins and tell them I would like to meet with their leader to sign it.
2	action	end
0	section	Attempting to talk to Sigmund
0	section	Talking to Duke Horacio again
1	line	Duke Horacio	Greetings. Welcome to my castle.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Have you any quests for me?
1	option	Where can I find money?
1	option	What was I doing again?
2	line	Player	What was I doing again?
2	line	Duke Horacio	You were taking the peace treaty to the cave goblins.
3	line	Player	I, er, lost the treaty.
3	line	Duke Horacio	*sigh* All right, here's another copy.
3	action	end
2	action	end
0	section	Delivering the treaty
1	line	Mistag	Hello, friend?
1	line	Player	I have a peace treaty from the Duke of Lumbridge.
1	line	Mistag	A peace treaty? Then you will not invade?
1	line	Player	No. As long as you stick to the terms of this treaty there will be no conflict. The Duke of Lumbridge wants to meet your ruler to sign it.
1	line	Mistag	I will summon Ur-tag, our headman, at once.
0	section	Cut scene: A meeting of leaders
1	box	~ The Signing of the Lumbridge-Dorgeshuun Treaty ~
1	line	Player	Your grace, I present Ur-tag, headman of the Dorgeshuun.
1	line	Duke Horacio	Welcome, Ur-tag. I am sorry that your race came under suspicion.
1	line	Duke Horacio	I assure you that the warmongering element has been dealt with.
1	line	Ur-tag	I apologize for the damage to your cellar. I will send workers to repair the hole.
1	line	Duke Horacio	No, let it stay. It can be a route of commerce between our lands.
1	line	Duke Horacio	{player}, Lumbridge is in your debt. Please accept this ring as a token of my thanks.
1	line	Duke Horacio	It is enchanted to save you in your hour of need.
1	line	Ur-tag	I too thank you. Accept the freedom of the Dorgeshuun mines.
1	line	Ur-tag	These are strange times. I never dreamed that I would see the surface, still less that I would be on friendly terms with its people.
1	line	Sigmund	Prattle on, goblin.
1	line	Sigmund	Soon you will be destroyed!
